  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Slide together",
  "description": "Mark out an area of about 40 × 30 metres with cones on the ice. Three red defenders stand in a line across it. Three blue players stand around them – one on each side and one in the middle behind – and a fourth blue, D, stands at the far end. Blue must make at least three passes, then try to play a firm pass along the ice past the defenders to D. Lofted balls do not count.\n\nRed are not allowed to win the ball at first. The defender nearest the ball carrier steps out and steers, and the other two slide across and cover so the gaps between them do not grow. When the ball is out wide, everyone shifts to that side; when it is central, they squeeze into the middle.\n\nBuild it up: red may win the ball and then score by passing to their own player at the other end. Swap jobs within and between the teams after a few minutes. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest player steps out – the rest move with the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stay compact: keep the gaps small so no pass goes straight through."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Move while the ball is travelling, not once it has arrived."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Steer the ball carrier out wide with your stick, away from the pass to D."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
